// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
// "What you still need to do" after an import.
//
// The import summary (importSummary.ts) tells an owner what we KEPT, REBUILT
// and DROPPED. That is a receipt, and a receipt is not a to-do list: a source
// site that loaded an Adobe Fonts kit imports "successfully" and then renders
// in a fallback face until somebody adds the new domain to that kit - and
// nothing in the product ever said so.
//
// This module reads the SOURCE page for signals we can honestly act on, and
// turns them into a small, ordered list of concrete follow-ups. Rules:
//   - every action names the thing to do, not the thing that happened
//   - never invent work: a signal we did not actually see produces no action
//   - "blocker" is reserved for things that stop a publish; everything an owner
//     can ship without is "action" or "info"
//
// Pure + presentation-agnostic (same reason as importSummary): the preview
// panel, the post-import screen and the import report all render this list.
// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

